    "summary": "Back-pack (&quot;kayabang&quot;) (with carrying strap); made of bamboo; a) back-pack: four slats of wood lashed together with piece of bamboo in each corner to make square frame at bottom; weft slats of bamboo rise up from base and extend outward, with strips of bamboo woven using wicker-work technique through slats; piece of bamboo bent and lashed together to make circular frame at top; b) tumpline (&quot;kayaban&quot;): thick strip of plaited bamboo, tapering at each end to loop; braided length of bamboo attached through loops and knotted together to tie strap to back-pack.",
